{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed2094082456/8/codegen_prompts/3.md\"","aggregated_output":"你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。\n\n## 新题位置\n\n- 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/8`\n- 题号：`3`\n- 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed2094082456/8/3.py`\n\n## 新题描述\n\n<new_puzzle index=\"3\">\n- `description`：根据种子像素在封闭区域内的相对位置，选择不同的填充图案对该区域进行铺设。\n- `Input structure`：背景色为黑色。网格中有若干用灰色线条围成的封闭矩形区域（灰色像素构成完整的矩形边框）。每个封闭区域内部恰好有一个单像素的彩色种子点。网格某个角落有一个图例区域，用红色边框围出，内部展示了三种填充图案样本：水平条纹（交替行填色）、垂直条纹（交替列填色）和棋盘格（交替像素填色），每种图案用不同的位置布局示意——种子点分别位于样本区域的顶部、中部、底部。\n- `Rule`：\n  - 判断每个封闭区域中种子像素的垂直位置：若种子在区域上三分之一，选择水平条纹图案；若在中间三分之一，选择棋盘格图案；若在下三分之一，选择垂直条纹图案。\n  - 用种子像素的颜色和所选图案填充整个封闭区域的内部背景像素（种子像素本身保留）。\n  - 图例区域在输出中保持不变。\n- `Key insight`：种子像素承担双重角色——它的颜色决定填充色，它在封闭区域内的相对垂直位置决定填充图案的类型。解题者需要同时从图例中归纳出三种图案与位置的对应关系，再应用到每个区域。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n## 机制相似参考题\n\n下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：先用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，再按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。\n\n已选参考：eval/dbff022c, eval/88e364bc, train/5adee1b2, train/2e65ae53, train/8a6d367c, train/34cfa167, eval/332f06d7, train/98c475bf\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"1\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"dbff022c\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3506\nmechanism=0.4056\nlexical=0.0137\ncode_feature=0.6000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, object:closed_region, object:frame, object:template, operation:flood_fill, relation:direction, relation:inside, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/dbff022c.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/dbff022c.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nFill hollow sprites' interiors using a color-palette legend on the grid edge.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color. Several hollow sprites with distinct border colors.\n- A small 2×N or N×2 palette block sits on one grid edge; one row/column lists border colors, the other lists corresponding fill colors.\n\nRule:\n- Locate the palette legend on a grid edge and read it as a border→fill color mapping.\n- Find enclosed bg regions (holes) inside sprites that don't touch the grid boundary.\n- For each hole, identify the most common adjacent border color, look it up in the palette, and fill the hole with the mapped fill color.\n\nKey insight: The palette's edge position and orientation determine reading direction; border colors in the palette uniquely key into fill colors.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"summary\": \"Use a color palette legend on the grid edge to fill sprites' interiors based on their border color mapping.\",\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"hollow sprites with colored borders s\",\n  \"dst\": \"interior of same sprite d\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"d.fill_color == palette_lookup(s.border_color)\",\n  \"path\": \"\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"\",\n  \"transform\": \"fill d with palette[s.border_color]\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": \"palette is 2xN or Nx2 block on grid edge; read direction based on edge position: top edge reads top-to-bottom, bottom edge reads bottom-to-top, left edge reads left-to-right; first row/column is border color, second is fill color\",\n  \"multi_step\": \"Step 1: locate 2xN or Nx2 palette legend on grid edge; Step 2: build color mapping (border -> fill) based on reading direction; Step 3: for each hollow sprite, lookup border color in palette and fill interior with corresponding fill color\",\n  \"concepts\": [\n    \"color-mapping\",\n    \"lookup-table\",\n    \"flood-fill\",\n    \"border-detection\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"The challenge is correctly reading the palette legend based on its edge position and orientation\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"88e364bc\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3469\nmechanism=0.4303\nlexical=0.0141\ncode_feature=0.4286\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, object:closed_region, object:frame, object:marker, object:rectangle, object:template, relation:direction, relation:inside, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/88e364bc.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/88e364bc.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nSlide yellow pixels inside walled regions in the direction dictated by border-legend arrows.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color; yellow pixels sit inside enclosed regions bounded by colored walls.\n- Border legends: small rectangles on the grid edge whose fill color C matches a region's border color. Each legend contains a center dot and an indicator dot encoding a direction.\n\nRule:\n- For each enclosed region, identify its border color C and look up the legend with fill color C.\n- The direction from the legend's center dot to its indicator dot gives the slide direction.\n- All yellow pixels in that region slide in that direction, stacking against the far wall.\n\nKey insight: Legend fill color links to region border color; the center→indicator offset encodes the movement vector.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"summary\": \"Yellow pixels inside colored-border regions move in the direction indicated by the red pixel in the legend with matching background color, stopping at region boundary.\",\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"yellow pixels inside colored-border regions s\",\n  \"dst\": null,\n  \"match_cond\": \"\",\n  \"path\": \"move(s, direction=legend.red_pixel_offset) where legend.background_color == s.containing_region.border_color until s.touches(region_boundary)\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"\",\n  \"transform\": \"\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": \"legend on grid edge with background color C and red pixel indicates: yellow pixels in regions with border color C move in direction from blue center to red pixel\",\n  \"multi_step\": \"\",\n  \"concepts\": [\n    \"legend/control-pixels\",\n    \"region-membership\",\n    \"directional-movement\",\n    \"boundary-collision\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"5adee1b2\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2868\nmechanism=0.3469\nlexical=0.0145\ncode_feature=0.4000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:closed_region, object:marker, object:rectangle, object:template, output:same_size, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5adee1b2.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/5adee1b2.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nUse the left-edge color legend to draw a padded rectangular halo around each matching object while preserving enclosed holes.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid has a dominant background color.\n- One or more two-row markers sit on the left edge; each marker is a 2x2 block whose left column is an object color and right column is its halo color.\n- Away from the markers, every source color from the legend appears as one or more 4-connected monochrome objects.\n\nRule:\n- Keep the input pixels unchanged.\n- For each source-color object, take its tight bbox expanded by one cell and clipped to the grid.\n- Recolor background pixels in that expanded region to the marker's halo color, except for background holes enclosed by the object.\n\nKey insight:\n- The small left-edge bars are a legend: they map object colors to the colors used for the surrounding padded bbox.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"4-connected monochrome objects on the background plus left-edge two-column color legend markers\",\n  \"transform\": \"for each object whose color appears in the legend, fill background pixels in its one-cell padded bbox with the paired legend color; preserve the object and any enclosed background holes\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": \"left-edge two-column legend maps object color to bbox-fill color\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"2e65ae53\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2711\nmechanism=0.3355\nlexical=0.0149\ncode_feature=0.3333\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:frame, object:rectangle, output:same_size, relation:inside, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/2e65ae53.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/2e65ae53.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nFill every lattice slot from the color assigned to that slot position by the other lattices.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- The largest foreground color forms several one-pixel-thick rectangular lattice frames.\n- The frame lines divide each lattice into the same row-by-column set of rectangular slots; some slots already contain one non-frame color.\n\nRule:\n- Infer a color for each logical slot position from the colored slots across all lattice frames.\n- Repaint every slot interior in every lattice with the inferred color for its row/column position.\n- Keep the frame lines and all background outside frames unchanged.\n\nKey insight:\n- Slot sizes vary by frame, but the complete color pattern is indexed by lattice slot position rather than by absolute pixel size or location.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"colored slot s in any lattice frame\",\n  \"dst\": \"slot interior d in any lattice frame\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"s.logical_slot_position == d.logical_slot_position\",\n  \"transform\": \"fill d with s.color, preserving frame lines and outside background\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"8a6d367c\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2561\nmechanism=0.3016\nlexical=0.0149\ncode_feature=0.4000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:frame, object:marker,